The input you provided is already in JSON format. Therefore, there is no need to convert it into another JSON format. 

However, if you want to make some modifications or add new fields to the JSON object, here is an example of how you can do it:

```json
{
    "output_list": [
        {
            "function_name": "ERC20",
            "vulnerability": "None",
            "criticism": "No vulnerable functions found.",
            "correctness": 9,
            "severity": 0,
            "profitability": 0,
            "recommendation": "This contract follows the ERC20 standard without any major vulnerabilities."
        }
    ]
}
```

In this example, we added a new field `recommendation` which gives a general recommendation based on the analysis.